  "description": "SS11.1 control - the same alpha-corpus images, flattened to opaque and encoded in the format's opaque mode. The alpha corpus is cut-outs, insignia and line art, and the graphics corpus independently prefers more luma than photographs do; without this control, 'alpha mode wants a different layout' and 'this content wants a different layout' are the same measurement. If the opaque optimum on these images sits near the photographic optimum, the alpha-mode shift belongs to alpha mode; if it moves the same way, it belongs to the content.",
